    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d678">

                <pb facs="1080" n="960" sameAs="frus:frus1932v01/pg960"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">196.6/1152</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Swedish Legation to the Department of State </hi>
                </head>
                <p>A bill has been introduced by Senator LaFollette numbered S. 1558 and entitled:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“A Bill to amend certain laws relating to American Seamen, and for other
                                purposes”.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d678-f1"/>
                        </p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Reference is made to the memorandum of this Legation dated January 14, 1932,
                    concerning the bill 1559, introduced by Senator LaFollette. It would seem that
                    the same arguments set forth in that memorandum can be applied in opposition to
                    the passage of the above mentioned bill No. 1558.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1932-04-04">April 4,
                            1932</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d678-f1" n="5" xml:id="d678-f1-content">
                <p>Introduced December 14, 1931; see <hi rendition="#italic">Congressional
                        Record</hi>, vol. 75, pt. 1, p. 440.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
